  triage:title "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/lib.rs exceeds 1000-line ceiling with zero test code (RULE-003), round 5" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/lib.rs has regrown past the RULE-003 1000-line non-test ceiling. Confirmed live by quality-mgr (arch-qa reviewer, round 5 of QA-PHASE-AO2-FINAL-GATE): wc -l = 2917 total lines, #[cfg(test)] module starts at line 1080, so non-test code = 1079 lines, exceeding the 1000-line ceiling. Not covered by any prior round's waiver or fix -- this is new growth discovered at round 5. Same RULE-003 pattern as the already-fixed ARCH-QA-AO2-R3-001 (writer/ops.rs split). Fix: extract a cohesive section into a sibling module -- arch-qa suggests either the AO2.14 server-task lifecycle plumbing (ServerTaskInputs/DirectPeerServer/ServerTaskTerminationGuard) or the preflight/validate_* config helpers. Follow the same split pattern/verification precedent used for ARCH-QA-AO2-R3-001 (check that resolution's git history, commit 837c14dd997f5c180a4666d7594eba7a3b22313f, for precedent -- verify via wc -l AND the #[cfg(test)]-start-line, not just total file length, since a prior attempt on a similar finding this phase made the defect worse by adding tests instead of splitting)." ;
